title The refusal that named no cause
prompt the standing baton -- take the next agent-doable lap, Lindy-first and crux-first, in the core-infrastructure lane
rota lap 4596, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; advanced by hand from row 1 past the four rows peers read today, row 4 standing unread. Earth takes in the concrete fact at the door before any argument about it, and `TWO_ROOMS.md` in its fixed seat says the same thing for prose: a claim enters the checkable room only when a witness binds it. `%700` had an inference standing where an observation belonged, and the reason it could have no observation was a mechanism nobody had named.
think Reds first. The pin holds 15 rows, 8 OPEN, and `%700` is the one squarely in this lane: `tools/m/mantra_recall_tablecloth_query_wire.rish` answered red on one cold roster pass and green minutes later over one unchanged tree -- `tree_moved=no`, thirteen greens and one red in fifteen runs by hand. Its own last sentence is the whole problem: the cause is inference, never observation.
think Read the witness before theorising about it, and the concrete fact was at the door. Five bindings, each `assert VAR.ok else "<leg> failed"`, and the file mentions neither `.out` nor `.err` anywhere. Rishi's `run` captures both; the interpreter then discards them. So a flap could fire for a fortnight and leave, every time, one sentence naming which LEG refused and nothing about why.
think Proved the repair before reaching for it, in a two-line pen: `assert r.ok else "probe failed: ${r.err}"` over a command exiting 3 prints `probe failed: to-stderr`. Rishi interpolates a capture into an else message, so the reason travels only when the door closes -- no green-path noise at all, which is the whole difference from the third shape's repair, a `say` that prints on every run forever.
think Checked for an existing home rather than opening a new guard. `shim_reason` already holds three shapes of one law -- hand on your target's reason -- and all three require the reason to be forwarded and forwarded badly: wrong stream, wrong field, one line too late. A binding that never reports at all falls through every one of them. So the instrument grew a fourth reading rather than the tree growing a fourth instrument.
think Measured before writing a ceiling. 7,110 bindings across 1,699 of 2,485 tracked `.rish` sources are judged and never reported, 953 of them on the standing roster across 170 of its 326 guards. That size is the argument for a ratchet: a gate at zero would red every lap on a tree no lap can repair, which is a gate somebody turns off.
think Wrote the reading as one awk pass keyed on FILENAME, the way the third shape's already is. A first draft looped over every live binding per line and cost 10.2s over the corpus; pre-filtering on the two reporting forms brought it to 0.5s, which matters for a guard at `tier lap` on 326 guards' clock.
obs The partition is structural rather than careful, and it is proven in the pen: `late_say` wants a say to exist below the assert, `reason_lost` wants `${var.out}` interpolated, and this one wants neither a say nor an interpolation of either field. One fault can never pay twice, so one repair can never look like two.
obs A refusal that names its leg and drops its tool's sentence is not a small loss -- it is the difference between a flap a hand can diagnose and one that can only be guessed at. `%700` is the receipt: the guard fired, the evidence page was written, and the compiler's own words were already gone.
obs Twelve repeat runs of the repaired witness answered green twelve times, which at the ledger's own one-in-fifteen rate expects under one red -- so the flap stays unobserved and the instrument that will name it when it fires is what this lap actually landed.
obs Held still badly. I edited tracked files while my own cold pass was 71 guards in, which voids its digest -- the fourth firing of that shape on today's card, now the fifth. I stopped the voided pass with `fleet_call.sh --pid ... --signal TERM` rather than spending two more hours on a reading already void, and the helper refused all seven peer trees by name before it sent.
